1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,348
Everything you've written so far is seen from a bridge.

2
00:00:05,248 --> 00:00:06,987
One ship, one crew,

3
00:00:07,437 --> 00:00:09,611
one system at a time.

4
00:00:11,411 --> 00:00:14,020
There's another seat in this game.

5
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:17,093
The Admiral doesn't fly anything.

6
00:00:17,993 --> 00:00:21,472
The Admiral looks down on a whole system,

7
00:00:21,922 --> 00:00:25,400
builds on its worlds, and sends fleets out.

8
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,809
Today you write for that seat.

9
00:00:31,009 --> 00:00:34,922
And I have to start with some bad news,

10
00:00:35,372 --> 00:00:38,850
because I'd rather you heard it from me.

11
00:00:40,650 --> 00:00:46,302
The Admiral's game doesn't run in the universe you made in Lecture Two,

12
00:00:46,752 --> 00:00:48,926
not as things stand today.

13
00:00:50,726 --> 00:00:52,465
I did try it.

14
00:00:53,365 --> 00:00:55,539
I added the Admiral's library,

15
00:00:55,989 --> 00:00:57,728
I changed the mode,

16
00:00:58,178 --> 00:01:00,352
and I wrote the chapters.

17
00:01:01,252 --> 00:01:03,861
The game started, and nothing happened.

18
00:01:04,761 --> 00:01:07,804
There was no console and no error.

19
00:01:09,604 --> 00:01:13,952
That's a fault in how two libraries find each other,

20
00:01:14,402 --> 00:01:16,141
and it's been reported.

21
00:01:17,041 --> 00:01:21,389
It isn't something you can fix from your mission folder.

22
00:01:23,189 --> 00:01:27,102
So today, we work where the Admiral does run,

23
00:01:27,552 --> 00:01:31,030
which is inside the Open Universe mission itself.

24
00:01:31,930 --> 00:01:34,104
And what you write there

25
00:01:34,554 --> 00:01:38,467
is exactly what your own universe will take later.

26
00:01:39,667 --> 00:01:41,841
First, we make a copy.

27
00:01:42,741 --> 00:01:45,785
Never change the Open Universe folder itself,

28
00:01:46,235 --> 00:01:48,843
because an update will replace it.

29
00:01:50,643 --> 00:01:55,426
I copy it, paste it, and call the copy Admiral Lab.

30
00:01:57,226 --> 00:01:58,965
One warning about saves.

31
00:01:59,865 --> 00:02:04,213
A save is named after the universe, not the folder,

32
00:02:04,663 --> 00:02:08,576
so the lab and the real thing share one.

33
00:02:09,476 --> 00:02:13,389
If you've got a skirmish game you care about,

34
00:02:13,839 --> 00:02:16,448
move that file somewhere safe first.

35
00:02:17,648 --> 00:02:22,430
Here's the whole game, so you know what you're writing for.

36
00:02:24,230 --> 00:02:28,143
The Admiral selects a world, and builds a headquarters.

37
00:02:29,043 --> 00:02:30,783
Then comes an extractor,

38
00:02:31,233 --> 00:02:33,407
and ore starts coming in.

39
00:02:34,307 --> 00:02:36,915
Then an academy and a shipyard,

40
00:02:37,365 --> 00:02:40,409
and the shipyard offers officers to commission.

41
00:02:41,309 --> 00:02:44,787
Each officer gets a fleet of three ships.

42
00:02:45,687 --> 00:02:47,861
And a lab offers research.

43
00:02:49,661 --> 00:02:52,704
You don't write any of those buildings.

44
00:02:53,604 --> 00:02:56,213
They're the same in every universe.

45
00:02:57,113 --> 00:03:01,026
You write the worlds, the people, and the ladder.

46
00:03:02,226 --> 00:03:05,704
This is the arena file, and it's short.

47
00:03:06,604 --> 00:03:09,648
Here are its three kinds of world.

48
00:03:10,098 --> 00:03:12,707
I'm adding a fourth, above them.

49
00:03:14,507 --> 00:03:18,420
Yields is what one extractor brings in each minute.

50
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:24,102
Reserve is how much there is before the world runs dry.

51
00:03:25,902 --> 00:03:28,511
And here's the rule that matters.

52
00:03:29,411 --> 00:03:32,454
The home system always gets one world,

53
00:03:32,904 --> 00:03:38,122
and it's the first one in the file that never runs dry.

54
00:03:39,022 --> 00:03:40,761
I put mine first,

55
00:03:41,211 --> 00:03:44,254
so my Admiral starts on my world.

56
00:03:45,454 --> 00:03:49,802
Next come the dials, and there are three I'm setting.

57
00:03:50,702 --> 00:03:52,441
There's the starting ore,

58
00:03:52,891 --> 00:03:55,065
how many fleets at once,

59
00:03:55,515 --> 00:03:58,559
and no border raids while I'm learning.

60
00:04:00,359 --> 00:04:02,098
Now, an honest number.

61
00:04:02,998 --> 00:04:05,172
I wrote five hundred ore.

62
00:04:06,072 --> 00:04:08,680
The game started with six thousand.

63
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:14,393
Part of that is the mode, which is fair.

64
00:04:15,293 --> 00:04:17,033
But most of it

65
00:04:17,483 --> 00:04:21,830
is a test setting the game's makers left switched on.

66
00:04:22,730 --> 00:04:26,209
It runs the Admiral's economy eight times fast.

67
00:04:28,009 --> 00:04:30,183
So don't balance anything today.

68
00:04:31,083 --> 00:04:33,691
Write the numbers your story suggests,

69
00:04:34,141 --> 00:04:37,620
and tune them when that setting is gone.

70
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:42,298
Officers look like the captains from Lecture Eight,

71
00:04:42,748 --> 00:04:45,791
and their values are the same traits.

72
00:04:47,591 --> 00:04:51,070
Here, though, three of those traits do something.

73
00:04:51,970 --> 00:04:55,883
By the book means the fleet burns less gas.

74
00:04:56,783 --> 00:04:58,522
Resourceful means more salvage.

75
00:04:59,422 --> 00:05:02,465
Fearsome means it engages from farther out.

76
00:05:04,265 --> 00:05:06,439
Every other trait is character.

77
00:05:07,339 --> 00:05:09,078
It's who she is,

78
00:05:09,528 --> 00:05:13,007
for the day a crew talks to her.

79
00:05:14,207 --> 00:05:18,554
The arena has no research, so I'm adding the chapter.

80
00:05:19,454 --> 00:05:21,193
There are two steps.

81
00:05:22,093 --> 00:05:26,007
Each one has a cost, a time in seconds,

82
00:05:26,457 --> 00:05:28,196
and what it unlocks.

83
00:05:29,096 --> 00:05:31,704
The second one requires the first,

84
00:05:32,154 --> 00:05:35,198
and that's what makes it a ladder.

85
00:05:36,998 --> 00:05:38,737
Now I run lint.

86
00:05:39,637 --> 00:05:42,680
Two warnings were there before I started.

87
00:05:43,580 --> 00:05:46,189
And there are four new ones,

88
00:05:46,639 --> 00:05:50,987
saying the game doesn't read my costs or my times.

89
00:05:51,887 --> 00:05:53,626
It does read them.

90
00:05:54,076 --> 00:05:58,424
I watched it take the ore, and the forty seconds.

91
00:06:00,224 --> 00:06:04,137
There's a line that makes those warnings go away,

92
00:06:04,587 --> 00:06:08,065
and I'm asking you not to write it.

93
00:06:08,965 --> 00:06:12,443
It quietly turns forty seconds into forty minutes.

94
00:06:13,343 --> 00:06:17,691
So for today, six warnings is what done looks like.

95
00:06:18,891 --> 00:06:20,630
Now let's play it.

96
00:06:21,530 --> 00:06:27,183
On the start screen I pick the skirmish universe, and a new game.

97
00:06:28,983 --> 00:06:32,461
There's one world at home, and it's mine.

98
00:06:33,361 --> 00:06:35,100
I build a headquarters,

99
00:06:35,550 --> 00:06:39,898
then the extractor, the academy, the shipyard and the lab.

100
00:06:40,798 --> 00:06:42,537
The ore is climbing.

101
00:06:44,337 --> 00:06:46,946
The shipyard offers my officer first,

102
00:06:47,396 --> 00:06:50,004
by her name and her title.

103
00:06:50,904 --> 00:06:53,948
And the lab offers my first step,

104
00:06:54,398 --> 00:06:57,441
and then, once that's done, my second.

105
00:06:58,641 --> 00:07:00,380
Now it's your turn.

106
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:06,063
In the lab, write the world your own side starts on,

107
00:07:06,513 --> 00:07:10,426
then two officers, and a ladder of three steps.

108
00:07:12,226 --> 00:07:14,400
Keep them there for now.

109
00:07:15,300 --> 00:07:17,474
When the fault is mended,

110
00:07:17,924 --> 00:07:21,402
it's three small moves to bring them home,

111
00:07:21,852 --> 00:07:24,026
and they're on the page.

112
00:07:25,826 --> 00:07:29,304
The lecture after this one isn't ready yet,

113
00:07:29,754 --> 00:07:32,363
so go on to the capstone.
